# Every tool version the checks depend on, in one place.
#
# The Makefile includes this file and CI sources it, so a development
# machine and a runner resolve the same versions from the same line. Before
# this file the pins lived only in .github/workflows/check.yml's env block,
# which meant they existed on CI and nowhere else: LLVM_MAJOR was referenced
# at Makefile:41 and never defined there, so a development machine linted
# with whatever clang-tidy it happened to carry. That is how a tree that
# passed CI failed `make check` locally under LLVM 23.
#
# The format is the intersection of `make include` and `sh .` syntax: NAME=value,
# no spaces around =, no quotes, no expansion. Keep it that way or one of the
# two readers stops working. `make lint-pins` fails if a workflow hardcodes a
# version this file already carries.
#
# Bumping a checker is not a routine update. CLAUDE.md forbids adapting code
# or suppressions to an older checker, so a new major reports what it reports
# and the findings are work to do, not noise to silence. The scheduled job in
# .github/workflows/toolchain-pins.yml opens a pull request when an upstream
# release appears and never merges it; the pull request's own CI run is the
# measurement of what the bump costs.

# Analysis tools. These decide what the linters say, not what the library
# does; none of them ships in bin/chapulin.o.
LLVM_MAJOR=22
CPPCHECK_VERSION=2.21.0
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=0.11.0

# Proof tools. Verdicts are solver-independent, so kissat is a speed pin
# rather than a correctness one, but proof/results/*.log record the CBMC
# version that produced them and the reach floors are measured under it.
CBMC_VERSION=6.11.0
KISSAT_VERSION=rel-4.0.4

# Test-only dependencies. Both carry real CVEs upstream and neither is part
# of the library: OpenSSL backs test/e2e.sh's certificate recipes, and Go
# builds test/goecho. They are pinned because their behaviour moves — the
# runner's OpenSSL 3.0 predates the `x509 -req -not_before` flag docs/ca.md
# tells operators to use, and which curves Go offers by default changes
# between releases.
OPENSSL_VERSION=3.6.3
GO_VERSION=1.27.0
